# P2P Protocol Considerations

## Supported Protocols

Envy supports multiple P2P protocols:
- **BitTorrent/DHT**: Torrent file sharing with distributed hash table
- **Gnutella2 (G2)**: Decentralized P2P network
- **Gnutella**: Original Gnutella protocol
- **ED2K/eMule**: eDonkey2000 network
- **DC++**: Direct Connect protocol
- **HTTP/FTP**: Traditional file transfer

## Network Code Guidelines

### Timeout Handling
```cpp
// ✅ Good: Implement proper timeouts
bool ConnectWithTimeout(const CString& strHost, WORD nPort, DWORD dwTimeout) {
    // Set socket timeout
    DWORD dwTimeoutMs = dwTimeout;
    setsockopt(m_hSocket, SOL_SOCKET, SO_RCVTIMEO,
               (const char*)&dwTimeoutMs, sizeof(dwTimeoutMs));
    setsockopt(m_hSocket, SOL_SOCKET, SO_SNDTIMEO,
               (const char*)&dwTimeoutMs, sizeof(dwTimeoutMs));

    // Attempt connection with timeout
    // ...
}

// ❌ Bad: No timeout handling
bool Connect(const CString& strHost, WORD nPort) {
    // May hang indefinitely
    connect(m_hSocket, ...);
}
```

### Network Interruption Handling
```cpp
// ✅ Good: Handle network interruptions gracefully
bool DownloadChunk(const BYTE* pData, size_t nSize) {
    int nSent = 0;
    while (nSent < nSize) {
        int nResult = send(m_hSocket,
                          (const char*)(pData + nSent),
                          nSize - nSent, 0);
        if (nResult == SOCKET_ERROR) {
            DWORD dwError = WSAGetLastError();
            if (dwError == WSAEWOULDBLOCK || dwError == WSAEINTR) {
                // Retry after short delay
                Sleep(10);
                continue;
            }
            // Fatal error
            return false;
        }
        nSent += nResult;
    }
    return true;
}
```

### Data Validation
```cpp
// ✅ Good: Validate all received data
bool ProcessPacket(const BYTE* pBuffer, size_t nSize) {
    // Validate packet size
    if (nSize < MIN_PACKET_SIZE || nSize > MAX_PACKET_SIZE) {
        LogError(_T("Invalid packet size: %zu"), nSize);
        return false;
    }

    // Validate packet header
    if (pBuffer[0] != PACKET_MAGIC) {
        LogError(_T("Invalid packet magic"));
        return false;
    }

    // Validate checksum
    if (!VerifyChecksum(pBuffer, nSize)) {
        LogError(_T("Packet checksum failed"));
        return false;
    }

    return ProcessValidPacket(pBuffer, nSize);
}
```

### Rate Limiting
```cpp
// ✅ Good: Implement rate limiting
class CRateLimiter {
private:
    DWORD m_dwMaxBytesPerSecond;
    DWORD m_dwBytesThisSecond;
    DWORD m_dwSecondStart;

public:
    void LimitTransfer(size_t nBytes) {
        DWORD dwNow = GetTickCount();
        DWORD dwElapsed = dwNow - m_dwSecondStart;

        if (dwElapsed >= 1000) {
            // New second, reset counter
            m_dwBytesThisSecond = 0;
            m_dwSecondStart = dwNow;
        }

        if (m_dwBytesThisSecond + nBytes > m_dwMaxBytesPerSecond) {
            // Need to throttle
            DWORD dwWait = 1000 - dwElapsed;
            Sleep(dwWait);
            m_dwBytesThisSecond = 0;
            m_dwSecondStart = GetTickCount();
        }

        m_dwBytesThisSecond += nBytes;
    }
};
```

## BitTorrent Specific

### BEP Compliance
```cpp
// ✅ Good: Follow BitTorrent Enhancement Proposals
// BEP 3: The BitTorrent Protocol Specification
// BEP 5: DHT Protocol
// BEP 23: Tracker Returns Compact Peer Lists

class CBitTorrentClient {
    // Implement proper peer protocol
    bool HandleHandshake(const BYTE* pData, size_t nSize);
    bool HandlePiece(const BYTE* pData, size_t nSize);
    bool HandleRequest(const BYTE* pData, size_t nSize);

    // Support DHT
    bool ProcessDHTNode(const CString& strIP, WORD nPort);

    // Support PEX (Peer Exchange)
    bool ProcessPEXPeers(const std::vector<CPeerInfo>& peers);
};
```

### Torrent Data Handling
```cpp
// ✅ Good: Handle corrupted torrent data
bool LoadTorrentFile(const CString& strPath) {
    try {
        CTorrentFile torrent;
        if (!torrent.Load(strPath)) {
            theApp.Message(MSG_ERROR, _T("Failed to load torrent file"));
            return false;
        }

        // Validate torrent structure
        if (!torrent.Validate()) {
            theApp.Message(MSG_ERROR, _T("Invalid torrent file structure"));
            return false;
        }

        // Check for required fields
        if (torrent.GetInfoHash().IsEmpty()) {
            theApp.Message(MSG_ERROR, _T("Torrent missing info hash"));
            return false;
        }

        return true;
    }
    catch (const std::exception& e) {
        theApp.Message(MSG_ERROR, _T("Error loading torrent: %hs"), e.what());
        return false;
    }
}
```

## Security Considerations

### Input Validation
```cpp
// ✅ Good: Validate all network input
bool ProcessPeerMessage(const BYTE* pData, size_t nSize, const CPeerInfo& peer) {
    // Validate message size
    if (nSize > MAX_MESSAGE_SIZE) {
        LogSecurity(_T("Oversized message from peer %s"), (LPCTSTR)peer.GetAddress());
        DisconnectPeer(peer);
        return false;
    }

    // Validate message type
    if (pData[0] >= MAX_MESSAGE_TYPE) {
        LogSecurity(_T("Invalid message type from peer %s"), (LPCTSTR)peer.GetAddress());
        return false;
    }

    // Sanitize file paths
    CString strPath = ExtractPath(pData, nSize);
    if (!IsPathSafe(strPath)) {
        LogSecurity(_T("Unsafe path from peer: %s"), (LPCTSTR)strPath);
        return false;
    }

    return ProcessValidMessage(pData, nSize, peer);
}
```

### Path Sanitization
```cpp
// ✅ Good: Prevent directory traversal
bool IsPathSafe(const CString& strPath) {
    // Check for directory traversal attempts
    if (strPath.Find(_T("..")) != -1) {
        return false;
    }

    // Check for absolute paths
    if (strPath.GetLength() > 0 && strPath[0] == _T('\\')) {
        return false;
    }

    // Check for drive letters (should be relative)
    if (strPath.GetLength() > 1 && strPath[1] == _T(':')) {
        return false;
    }

    // Additional validation...
    return true;
}
```

## Protocol Compatibility

### Backward Compatibility
```cpp
// ✅ Good: Support multiple protocol versions
enum class ProtocolVersion {
    V1_0,
    V1_1,
    V2_0
};

bool HandleProtocolHandshake(const BYTE* pData, size_t nSize) {
    ProtocolVersion version = DetectVersion(pData, nSize);

    switch (version) {
        case ProtocolVersion::V1_0:
            return HandleV1_0Handshake(pData, nSize);
        case ProtocolVersion::V1_1:
            return HandleV1_1Handshake(pData, nSize);
        case ProtocolVersion::V2_0:
            return HandleV2_0Handshake(pData, nSize);
        default:
            LogError(_T("Unsupported protocol version"));
            return false;
    }
}
```

## Avoid

- Blocking network operations on UI thread
- Not validating network data
- Ignoring timeout errors
- Not handling network interruptions
- Unsafe path operations
- Not rate limiting operations
- Breaking protocol compatibility
